 "fields": [
  {
   "fieldname": "intro_html",
   "fieldtype": "HTML",
   "options": "<div class=\"text-muted\" style=\"padding:8px 0\">Use <b>Refresh Diff</b> to scan ERPNext source doctypes and rebuild every tab's field-mapping table. Resolve any rows whose <b>Action</b> is <b>Unresolved</b>, then click <b>Lock Mapping</b> to freeze the resolved entries into <a href=\"/app/crm-migration-field-map\">CRM Migration Field Map</a> — the runner consumes that table.</div><div class=\"alert alert-info\" style=\"margin-top:8px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:12px\"><b>Tip — pre-create matching custom fields on the CRM side.</b> If your ERPNext doctypes have custom fields you want migrated, add a custom field with the <b>same fieldname</b> on the corresponding Frappe CRM doctype <i>before</i> clicking Refresh Diff. Same-name fields are auto-mapped by the diff, so you avoid resolving each one manually. Mappings: Lead &rarr; CRM Lead, Opportunity &rarr; CRM Deal, Prospect &rarr; CRM Organization, Territory &rarr; CRM Territory, Industry Type &rarr; CRM Industry, UTM Source &rarr; CRM Lead Source, Opportunity Lost Reason &rarr; CRM Lost Reason, Item &rarr; CRM Product.</div>"
  },

